{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-113590",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The point $R$ corresponds to the number ${x}_{1}=-8$ while the midpoint $M$ corresponds to ${x}_{m}=-5.$\n\nTo find the number ${x}_{2}$ corresponding to the point $S$, we first set up an equation using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\ -5 & =\\frac{-8+{x}_{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & =\\frac{-8+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\ 2\\cdot (-5) & =-8+{x}_{2} \\\\ -10 & =-8+{x}_{2} \\\\ -2 & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $S$ corresponds to ${x}_{2}=-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14171842/assets/1db6d041dc8dcbba0e10cbe3dae582bbc2bf8bc1619e93946807c9deae598be3.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
